# AD-01: Domain Controller Setup & AD DS Installation — Verification & Baseline Audit

## Scenario

A newly provisioned Windows Server 2022 Domain Controller has been handed off for verification before any users or computers are added to the environment. The task is to audit the DC's health, confirm all critical services and components are functioning correctly, understand the default AD structure, and establish a documented baseline configuration — mirroring what a junior sysadmin would be expected to do when inheriting a new domain controller.

**Status:** Core verification completed successfully. Recurring BSOD instability identified during session — root cause isolated, fix pending next session.

